/*
TOWERS OF HANOI — a construction puzzle: the solution IS a move
sequence, and the timeline below performs it. Three disks, three
towers, 2^3 - 1 = 7 moves.

The rule of the game is ONE line of geometry: never a larger disk
resting on a smaller — `check never on(disk_3 disk_1)`. It survives
transit (a big disk sliding OVER a small one on its way past is not
resting on it), so the gate reads exactly what the puzzle means.
Try the falsifier: change move 3's destination from (0 0.4 0) to
(4 0.4 0) — disk_1 lands back on empty air where disk_2 no longer
is; or worse, send move 4's disk_3 down onto tower_b's stack and
watch the legality gate go red the instant it settles.

The disks are TUBES — genuinely hollow, so the pegs pass through the
bores instead of interpenetrating (hollowness is a fact, not a look).

And the closing goal is the whole thesis in one statement: the rules
layer DERIVES the 7-move plan by recursion — solve n-1 onto the
spare, move the big one, solve n-1 back on top — and the answer it
prints is move-for-move the sequence the animation performs. The
engine plans; the world performs; the checks referee.
*/

theme clay

// three towers as open zones — a disk is IN a tower only when it's
// down in the stack; mid-flight it is honestly nowhere
room tower_a size(3.2 1.4 3.2) walls(0) at(-4 0) color(#d8cfc2)
room tower_b size(3.2 1.4 3.2) walls(0) at(0 0) color(#d8cfc2)
room tower_c size(3.2 1.4 3.2) walls(0) at(4 0) color(#d8cfc2)

cylinder peg_a r(0.12) h(1.6) at(-4 0) color(#7a6a58)
cylinder peg_b r(0.12) h(1.6) at(0 0) color(#7a6a58)
cylinder peg_c r(0.12) h(1.6) at(4 0) color(#7a6a58)

// the disks: hollow rings threaded on the peg, largest at the bottom
tube disk_3 r(0.3) walls(0.95) h(0.4) sides(12) at(-4 0) color(#b25438)
tube disk_2 r(0.3) walls(0.65) h(0.4) sides(12) on(disk_3) color(#3d7fa6)
tube disk_1 r(0.3) walls(0.35) h(0.4) sides(12) on(disk_2) color(#b98a1d)

// ---- the solution: 7 moves, one beat after another --------------------
// `then` = after the previous move lands (the 1-second gap is pacing).
// No clock arithmetic anywhere: the story is a sequence, so the text
// is one. Reorder the blocks and you reorder the solution.
then 1
// move 1: disk_1 to tower_c
move disk_1 to(-4 2 0) over(1)
move disk_1 to(4 2 0) over(1)
move disk_1 to(4 0 0) over(1)
end

then 1
// move 2: disk_2 to tower_b
move disk_2 to(-4 2 0) over(1)
move disk_2 to(0 2 0) over(1)
move disk_2 to(0 0 0) over(1)
end

then 1
// move 3: disk_1 onto disk_2
move disk_1 to(4 2 0) over(1)
move disk_1 to(0 2 0) over(1)
move disk_1 to(0 0.4 0) over(1)
end

then 1
// move 4: disk_3 to tower_c — the big crossing, right over disk_1
move disk_3 to(-4 2 0) over(1)
move disk_3 to(4 2 0) over(1)
move disk_3 to(4 0 0) over(1)
end

then 1
// move 5: disk_1 back to tower_a
move disk_1 to(0 2 0) over(1)
move disk_1 to(-4 2 0) over(1)
move disk_1 to(-4 0 0) over(1)
end

then 1
// move 6: disk_2 onto disk_3
move disk_2 to(0 2 0) over(1)
move disk_2 to(4 2 0) over(1)
move disk_2 to(4 0.4 0) over(1)
end

then 1
// move 7: disk_1 crowns the tower
move disk_1 to(-4 2 0) over(1)
move disk_1 to(4 2 0) over(1)
move disk_1 to(4 0.8 0) over(1)
end

// ---- the rule of the game: these GATE every instant ------------------
check never on(disk_2 disk_1)
check never on(disk_3 disk_1)
check never on(disk_3 disk_2)

// ---- the tower is rebuilt --------------------------------------------
check always in(disk_3 tower_a) during(0 13)
check always in(disk_3 tower_c) during(16 30)
check always on(disk_2 disk_3) during(24 30)
check always on(disk_1 disk_2) during(28 30)

// ---- the derived story (scrub and watch) -----------------------------
? on(disk_1 disk_2)
? when on(disk_1 disk_2)
? when in(disk_1 tower_b)

// ---- the engine derives the plan the timeline performs ---------------
// solve n-1 onto the spare, move the big disk, solve n-1 back on top.
// Compare the answer to the move comments above: identical, in order.
?- assertz(hanoi(0, _, _, _, [])),
   assertz((hanoi(N, From, To, Via, Plan) :-
       N > 0, M is N - 1,
       hanoi(M, From, Via, To, First),
       hanoi(M, Via, To, From, Rest),
       append(First, [From-To|Rest], Plan))),
   hanoi(3, tower_a, tower_c, tower_b, Plan)
